                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "If you stretch the definition of multi-host a bit, it's a multi-host \nsystem with `n == 1` hosts. It's a matter of perspective and configuration i guess.\n\nOverall i have limited options for testing since i don't have a functional multi-host hardware with `n > 1` hosts.\n\nWhich is why i sometimes get creative with using whatever hw is available to me.\n\nI understand this behavior increases maintainer load, but that development approach (no access to real multi-host hw) is not something i can influence from my side.\n\nTesting with qemu yv4 would also be an option here but it does not make a difference for this specific bug and the qemu yv4 is pretty slow. Which means it's hard to run the full Tree Redfish Service Validator."
                },
